  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Speeding up of Universal Access to Prevention, Treament and Support Services - Botswana (01-Oct-2015-30-Sep-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Botswana, Malaria, Botswana-Ministry of Health (Ministry of Health)This program has the following goals: To achieve zero local malaria transmission in Botswana by 2018. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To develop a robust information system for tracking progress and decision making by 2016.  Objective 2: To effect behaviour change through reaching at least 90% of the population with appropriate information for malaria elimination by 2017.  Objective 3: To detect all malaria infection through appropriate diagnostic methods and provide effective treatment by 2016.  Objective 4: To achieve total coverage with all appropriate vector control interventions in all transmission foci by 2016.  Objective 5: By 2016,  develop the requisite capacity in the programme at all levels to achieve malaria elimination</narrative>
  </description>
